{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Patchset 2 — `Verified -1` root-caused; TWO distinct causes, not one\n\nChange 2652, patchset 2 = `4bba9fbb9ebf` (same Change-Id).\n\n### Cause 1 (mine, real, fixed): the announcement warning killed the xdist controller\n\nThe three pytest cells did NOT fail at collection. They ran, then died mid-run. Verbatim from\n`pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.11)`:\n\n```\nINTERNALERROR>   File \".../xdist/workermanage.py\", line 474, in unserialize_warning_message\nINTERNALERROR>     mod = importlib.import_module(data[\"message_module\"])\nINTERNALERROR> ModuleNotFoundError: No module named '_browser_tier'\n[gw0] node down: <ExceptionInfo ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named '_browser_tier'\")>\n...\nINTERNALERROR> KeyError: <WorkerController gw0>\n1 failed, 34 passed, 1 skipped in 78.56s\n```\n\nAn xdist worker serializes a warning by its **class's module name**, and the CONTROLLER\nre-imports that module to rebuild it. `BrowserTierNotRunWarning` was defined in\n`tests/e2e/_browser_tier.py`: importable on the worker (pytest puts `tests/e2e` on the\nworker's path when it loads that conftest) and **not** on the controller, whose path never\nincludes it. So the first licensed skip took the node down and cascaded into an\n`INTERNALERROR`. The mechanism built to make the tier's absence loud was loud enough to abort\nthe run announcing it — exactly the distinction between \"loud in the RESULT\" and \"loud enough\nto kill the session\".\n\nIt never showed locally because every verification run was single-process; the CI lane uses\n`-n 4 --dist worksteal`.\n\n**Reproduced locally, then fixed and re-verified:**\n\n```\npytest tests -n 2 --dist worksteal -k \"editor_renders_diagram_panel... or test_committed_record_is_complete\"\n  BEFORE: INTERNALERROR ModuleNotFoundError: No module named '_browser_tier'   (session dead)\n  AFTER:  1 passed, 7 skipped, 1 warning in 18.36s\npytest tests/e2e tests/unit/test_browser_tier_optout.py -n 2 --dist worksteal  ->  46 passed\n```\n\n**Fix:** the category is now `pytest.PytestWarning` — an installed class both ends can import,\nthe same channel `tests/conftest.py` already uses for its xdist-safe timing spans. The banner\nand the full recorded reasoning are unchanged, so AC4 still holds.\n\n**New regression test** `test_the_warning_category_is_importable_by_the_xdist_controller`\nprobes the invariant the way the controller does: an isolated interpreter (`python -I`, which\nignores cwd and `PYTHONPATH`) must be able to import the module the category is defined in.\nDemonstrated RED against the old design — restoring a tests-local category makes it fail with\n`the browser-tier warning category lives in '_browser_tier_under_test', which an xdist\ncontroller cannot import`.\n\n### Cause 2 (not mine, environmental): the bwrap sandbox cell\n\n`sandbox enforcement (Linux bwrap, gating)` failed with `Process completed with exit code 100`\nin the step `docker run --rm --privileged ubuntu:24.04 bash -c 'set -e; apt-get update -qq\n>/dev/null 2>&1; apt-get install -y -qq bubblewrap >/dev/null 2>&1; ...'`. 100 is apt-get's\nerror code, and the step suppresses all apt output, so the log shows only the exit. The step\nruns a stock `ubuntu:24.04` container and installs from the Ubuntu archive; it reads nothing\nfrom the patchset, and this change touches only `tests/`, `docs/` and one YAML comment. The\nsame job was `success` on run `33938327905` eight minutes earlier. So: a transient package-\nmanager fault, not a second defect and not a consequence of cause 1. No `recheck` was posted —\npatchset 2 re-runs CI anyway.\n\nWorth noting as a separate observation: that step's `>/dev/null 2>&1` means an apt failure\nhere can never say why. Same shape as this ticket — a gate whose failure is unreadable.\n\nNot closed, not submitted.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788577061104440734,"uuid":"bbeb5faa-7f1c-4938-92a1-3f9317bc8a5d"}